From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:56:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Make the player visibility map thread-safe

CraftPlayer#onEntityRemove is called for every online player from the
thread of the region that removes the entity, and canSee is read by other
regions' trackers and the player list, while hideEntity/showEntity write
the same HashMap from the player's region. Concurrent access corrupted
the map and crashed regions with ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException during
rehash on servers that use the vanish API.

Use a ConcurrentHashMap; reads stay lock-free on the hot canSee path.

Fixes PaperMC/Folia#406
Related: PaperMC/Folia#448

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftPlayer.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftPlayer.java
index 24f7cf40ffd6bbb154dc664bc9f7e6661247f2ac..f3ec95b3a2fce21c347983ef9e9752b4d89f1b39 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftPlayer.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftPlayer.java
@@ -241,7 +241,7 @@ public class CraftPlayer extends CraftHumanEntity implements Player, PluginMessa
     private long lastPlayed = 0;
     private boolean hasPlayedBefore = false;
     private final ConversationTracker conversationTracker = new ConversationTracker();
-    private final Map<UUID, Set<WeakReference<Plugin>>> invertedVisibilityEntities = new HashMap<>();
+    private final Map<UUID, Set<WeakReference<Plugin>>> invertedVisibilityEntities = new java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap<>(); // Tessera - removed and read from other regions' threads
     private final Set<UUID> unlistedEntities = new HashSet<>(); // Paper - Add Listing API for Player
     private static final WeakHashMap<Plugin, WeakReference<Plugin>> pluginWeakReferences = new WeakHashMap<>();
     private int hash = 0;
